OL,3,GNEWSAMan, 80, who died in light
OL,4,Aaircraft crash near Loch Lomond named
OL,5,
OL,6,FAn 80-year-old man who died in a light
OL,7,Faircraft crash is understood to be
OL,8,Fflying instructor Ian Haggis.
OL,10,FHe and a 16-year-old boy died when
OL,11,Ftheir plane came down near Loch Lomond.
OL,12,FThe teenager's identity has not been
OL,13,Freleased.
OL,15,FThe pair had flown out from Glasgow
OL,16,FAirport at 16:17 and stopped
OL,17,Ftransmitting at 16:37, a few miles
OL,18,Fnorth east of the village of Drymen
OL,19,Fnear Stirling.
OL,21,FEmergency services were called to the
OL,22,Fcrash at about 16:45 on Friday.
OL,23,APub: 18-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
